<title>USA: Western Pacific starts Orlando service.</title>
<headline>Western Pacific starts Orlando service.</headline>
<dateline>COLORADO SPRINGS, Colo. 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Western Pacific Airlines said it began service to Orlando, Fla., on Friday.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that the introductory one-way fare from Colorado Springs, Western Pacific's base, to Orlando was $99. The one-way coast-to-coast connecting introductory fare is $119.</p>
<p>The introductory fares are valid for travel from Sept 6 to Sept 19.</p>
<p>-- New York newsroom, (212) 859-1610</p>
